# Versioning

There is **one** number, everywhere: **Version x.y.z** (`package.json` `"version"`, changelog headings, tags `vx.y.z`, replies). Never a second label for the same release (no “also 1.2.5”).

After each finished user task, bump **before** you stop. Skip typo-only edits, or if they say not to. Chats are not versions until the work lands.

**Ship without asking.** After the bump lands in `package.json` + `CHANGELOG.md`, commit, push `HEAD` to `miltoncwlam` `ai-flashcard`, and push annotated tag `vx.y.z` to `miltoncwlam` and `origin`. Do not wait for “commit/push/tag?”. Do not force-push `origin/milton`. Skip only if they said not to ship.

**Do not tell the user it shipped until production is live.** After push, wait until GitHub Actions `quality` on `miltoncwlam` `ai-flashcard` is **success** for that commit, then until Vercel production (`https://hkstudya.vercel.app`) is **Ready** for it. Only then reply **Version x.y.z**. If `quality` or Vercel fails, fix and bump again — stay quiet about the version until both are green.

```text
❌ BAD: tag pushed, then immediately “Version 3.9.1”
✅ GOOD: quality + Vercel Ready, then “Version 3.9.2”
```

## How far to bump

| Kind | Bump | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Major** | **x+1.0.0** | Full-version change: new core product, breaking auth/API, removed main feature |
| **Minor** | **x.y+1.0** | New capability (studio tile, play mode, auth flow) |
| **Miniscule** | **x.y.z+1** | Bugfix, copy, reliability, docs |

Never skip or reuse a number. One task → one bump.

## Log

Only [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md). Prepend:

```markdown
## Version x.y.z — YYYY-MM-DD
`abc1234`
```

Then detailed Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed (what, why, what the user sees). Reply **Version x.y.z** only after the production deploy succeeded.

```text
❌ BAD: “v1.5.0 (same as 1.2.6)”
✅ GOOD: Version 3.1.0 — Account Portal; next Clerk fix is 3.1.1
```
